                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "On the birght side, I actually found that the movement felt more fluid in this one and that the environment, while still generally poor visually, was a lot easier to understand than in the previous game. \n\n\nThe real downfall is the puzzles and the story, which are so extraordinarily bad.   Its all just so bizarre and unpleasant.  None of it feels like it fits together well either; all out of place and haphazardly formed. \n\nI feel like I would probably recommend Elansar over this one, but I would recommend almost anything over Elansar.   Sadly, the minor improvements were overshadowed by a cofusing setting and lack of coherence.",
